// Title: KScript statements shown in workspace/inspector screenshots (bubble construction)
// Author: not credited on the figure pages
// Source: VPRI TR-2012-001 (STEPS 2012 final report), three screenshot figures:
//         (a) "Rounding the corners, etc." (boxBubble inspector), PDF page 9 (printed page 8);
//         (b) "Customizing a part within the bubble to be a text editor" (KSBox(nameWatcher, 7@7)), PDF page 9;
//         (c) "Setting up one of the bubble's command buttons" (pickupButton), PDF page 10 (printed page 9).
// Transcribed from the page images; these are workspace text shown in screenshots, not program listings in the
// text layer; text-layer differences noted below.

// (a) boxBubble workspace, figure "Rounding the corners, etc."
this.cornerRadius(8)
this.borderFill(this.factory.theme.edgeColor)
this.borderWidth(1)

// (b) KSBox(nameWatcher, 7@7) workspace, figure "Customizing a part within the bubble to be a text editor"
this.beLineEditor()
this.fill(Color.transparent())
this.borderWidth(1)

// (c) pickupButton workspace, figure "Setting up one of the bubble's command buttons"
this.enteredFill = this.factory().buttonGradient()
this.textContents("pick up")
this.actionID = "box pick up"

// Transcription notes
// - [?] Figure (a) and (b) lines are partly covered by the inspector's scroll area and the mouse cursor;
//   the trailing ")" of "this.borderWidth(1)" is partly obscured by the text cursor in both figures.
//   Kept as the visible text.
// - Figure (c) is legible; the text cursor marks the end of its last line.
// - Pixel-level screenshots: spacing and capitalisation as seen; the figures are low resolution.
